[i]If you enjoy this mod, please rate it! Thank you.[/i]

[h1]Arcane Power[/h1]

[i]There is something moving inside the containment field.
The instruments call it a reaction. The engineers call it a power source.
Neither explanation makes the emergency shutters feel thick enough.[/i]

You have learned how to wake it. You have learned how to draw power from it.
[b]Make sure you also learn how to let it go.[/b]

Build an industrial arcane power plant: mine rare fuel, maintain its containment, recover heat through a modular Brayton cycle and bank the electricity. Keep an escape route for the core when containment fails.

[h2]The Reactor[/h2]

[list]
[*]One large-grid [b]Arcane Reactor[/b] with animated assembly, rotating rings, tile replacement and core ejection
[*][b]20% standalone efficiency[/b], or [b]40% starter / up to 78% exotic Brayton[/b] with eligible fuel, turbines and cooling
[*][b]Aether only in standalone[/b]; Helion and Empyrean require Brayton
[*]Two functional controllers provide 2/3/4 rings; [b]at least one advanced controller unlocks Brayton[/b]
[*]Demand-based fuel use, gradual ramp, grid-powered containment and a shutdown reserve
[*]Manifolds retract behind curved sliding panels; mode changes wait for shutdown and cooling
[/list]

[h2]Build a Brayton Plant[/h2]

Build up to [b]four independent circuits[/b], each with one turbine and its own cooling. One to four complete circuits provide [b]25/50/75/100% capacity[/b] at their normal tier efficiency. Keep reactor outlets separate, align H/C bores, use reactor adapters and cap unused pipe mouths. Build on one physical large grid; conveyors and subgrids cannot carry heat.

[list]
[*]One duplex pipe family with framed/bare straights, elbows, risers, tees, crosses, adapters and caps
[*]Standard/upgraded turbines, regular/mirrored, [b]2 wide x 2 high x 5 long[/b] with one lower socket
[*]Reflective glass, animated flow, spinning blades and a copper-wound armature behind inspection windows
[*]Built-in compressors and reactor-generated CO2; no separate tank, generator, heater or recuperator
[/list]

Complete circuits are ready immediately, with [b]no filling or pressure gate[/b]. Each Aether circuit requests [b]125 MW for cold compressor startup and hot shutdown circulation[/b], plus containment. Partial delivery gives reduced circulation. Adding/removing blocks and repairing connections updates circuit validity even while the reactor is off. Repairs and reloads require no refilling. Old shared plants migrate disabled with heat retained: separate their circuits and restart. Replace older oversized turbines and reroute two-socket trains to the lower socket.

Atmospheric coolers fit a [b]3x3x2-cell hull opening[/b], with rear manifolds. Leave [b]2.5 m beyond both fan guards[/b]: half-clear exhaust gives 25% cooling; blocked fans give none.

Space radiators connect underneath and track edge-on to the sun. Stack up to [b]two extensions[/b] on the same grid: aim at the top shaft coupling and match the base Up axis; [b]any yaw works[/b]. The guide marks the dock and tilt correction. Grind either panel face to remove a section. Keep the 3x3-cell sweep and both faces clear. Each panel retains [b]100/75/50% cooling at 0/50/100% sun[/b], including shade/weather. Faint red-orange glow follows actual rejection; detached/excess panels add no cooling.

Standard coolers/panels reject [b]10 GW each[/b], upgraded units [b]100 GW[/b]. Three equally exposed radiator sections provide 30/300 GW; mixed stacks add each rating. Compare Cooling capacity/required on the Power page. Shortfalls store waste: heat warns at 100%, with irreversible failure at [b]125%[/b]. Restore cooling or stop early; retain cooldown power.

Reactor shut-offs open each complete checked circuit even while cold or unfilled, and close invalid/unused circuits. The reactor adapter's offset end connects only to the vessel; use its opposite end for normal pipes. Losing all valid circuits stops generation; repair and restart manually. [b]Only a manual Start with all four circuits defective latches a circuit-loss fault.[/b] One valid circuit allows startup, even before pressure builds. Normal Stop and cooldown do not latch. Stored heat and an armed fuse remain. Repaired circuits can refill for cooldown while off. Advanced-controller loss stops Brayton generation, retaining connected cooling. No automatic standalone fallback.

[h2]Feed the Field[/h2]

Mine asteroid Aetherite, Helionite and Empyrite; refine concentrates and fill crafted canisters with Aether, then upgrade to Helion and Empyrean. Spent fuel returns no canister.

Aether recovers [b]10 Aether Residuum per canister[/b] in either mode. Upgraded turbines need [b]20 units[/b], upgraded coolers/panels [b]10[/b]. Fractional/blocked recovery survives saves; conveyors can export it. Empyrean requires upgraded turbines.

The [b]80-tile shell[/b] accepts mixed Standard/Reinforced/Advanced tiles with increasing lifetimes. Conveyors replenish fuel and tiles. Shutdown retains the shell; [b]ejection loses it[/b]. Neglect increases wear, fuel use and failure risk.

[h2]Give It a Way Out[/h2]

Fit [b]1-15 aligned vent ducts and an outlet[/b] above the reactor. Keep the outlet clear and point it somewhere expendable. Manual ejection and automatic ejection at 60% integrity require working controllers, route and actuation power/reserve. Broken routes pause launch while heat and critical timers continue. Security mode shuts down generation if the vent route is lost.

[b]Ejecting a critical core moves the danger. It does not cancel it.[/b]

[h2]Arcane Energy Core[/h2]

A [b]3x3x3 battery[/b] stores [b]1,000 MWh[/b] at [b]10 GW[/b]. Two capacity sockets add 10,000 MWh per standard module or 100,000 MWh per advanced module. A rear transfer module raises the ceiling to 100 GW or 1 TW. A front stabilizer reduces upkeep and ability recovery for matching/lower tiers.

[list]
[*]Native Auto/Recharge/Discharge modes with 90% charging efficiency
[*]Emergency reserve available to eligible reactors
[*][b]Burst discharge[/b]: double output for ten seconds
[*][b]Jump-drive surge[/b]: spend stored energy to accelerate one drive; normal jump restrictions apply
[*]Shared ability recovery, reactor-support priority and animated charge indicators
[/list]

Align 1x3x1 modules on the same grid. Detached cells retain charge/upkeep; destruction loses charge; copied/projected/new storage starts empty. Vanilla batteries also provide startup/backup power.

[h2]Know What Is Happening[/h2]

Placement arrows, H/C markers and construction instructions identify bad joints, missing welds and machines. [b]Solid red pipe rings[/b] warn of disconnected or invalid circuits. Each complete circuit restores its own colours, including capped ends; one complete circuit permits startup at 25% capacity while the other three remain incomplete. Valid idle circuits show amber status and pumping circuits show green. Verify power, fuel and cooling too. Monitor the terminal, [b]Arcane Reactor[/b] LCD or read-only antenna-linked tablet. Text HUD API is optional; native fallback is included.

[h2]Getting Started[/h2]

[olist]
[*]Enable the mod in an experimental world; find blocks under [b]Arcane Systems[/b].
[*]Weld the reactor, fit two controllers and complete its duct/outlet stack.
[*]Supply external power, Aether and tiles; start in standalone.
[*]For Brayton, fit an advanced controller, stop/cool the reactor, select the mode, wait for deployment and build independent circuits using the guide.
[*]Resolve interlocks, enable the reactor and allow startup to complete. Connect electrical demand or storage.
[/olist]

[h2]Compatibility and Development[/h2]

Works independently of Ship Core Framework, Arcane Cores and Animation Engine. Models, icons, weld stages and LODs are included.

[b]Alpha:[/b] live Brayton commissioning, save/load, multiplayer and balance remain unverified. Recipes are provisional; moving vent-door collision and arbitrary outlet-obstruction checks are unfinished.

